---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Components
description: All Lily Design System components, rendered via Nunjucks macros and styled in NHS UK visual tokens.
---

{% if components | length == 0 %}
<p>
  No components are implemented yet in the headless Nunjucks project.
  See
  <a href="https://github.com/lilydesignsystem/lily-design-system/tree/main/lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless">
  lily-design-system-nunjucks-headless</a> to add one.
</p>
{% else %}
{#
  Plan P6-T5: category + suffix-pattern filters alongside the existing
  free-text search, ported from the canonical SvelteKit reference
  (lily-design-system-svelte-sveltekit-examples/src/routes/components/+page.svelte).

  This app is a static site with progressive-enhancement JS (see
  AGENTS.md: "pages work without JS"), and unlike the other six ports
  this page shipped with *no* client-side search at all before this
  change. A search box and two <select>s that silently did nothing
  without JavaScript would be worse than no controls -- so the filter
  panel itself is not part of this server-rendered markup. Instead this
  renders the plain, fully-working static list exactly as before, and
  src/assets/js/modules/components-search.js injects the entire filter
  panel (search input, category select, suffix-pattern select, clear
  button, live result count) only once it actually runs, replacing the
  static count paragraph below.

  Each <li> carries data-category server-side, sourced from the root
  canonical components-categories.tsv via src/_data/components.js.
  data-suffix is computed client-side from the slug by the JS module,
  which is also where the suffix-pattern derivation logic lives (ported
  verbatim from src/lib/data/suffix-pattern.ts) -- kept in one place
  rather than duplicated into a Nunjucks filter.
#}
<div data-module="components-search" id="components-search">
  <script type="application/json" id="component-categories-data">{{ componentCategories | dump | safe }}</script>

  <p id="components-count">
    {{ components | length }} component{% if components | length != 1 %}s{% endif %} currently implemented.
  </p>

  <ul class="component-index-list" id="component-index-list">
    {% for c in components %}
    <li class="component-index-list-item" data-category="{{ c.category }}">
      <a href="/components/{{ c.kebab }}/">{{ c.title }}</a>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
</div>
{% endif %}
